{
  "id": 442994194,
  "iid": 22951,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "TCP: align flag characters with those used in tcpdump",
  "description": "Both Wireshark and tcpdump have flag characters to indicate TCP flags.\nThis change brings into alignment the CWR flag. tcpdump uses 'W' here,\nfor \"Window\", rather than 'C' for \"Congestion\". Start using the same\nin Wireshark.\n\nThis leaves out the '.' character used by tcpdump for the ACK flag.\nIn the Wireshark representation of the flags string, the distinction\nbetween the dot (indicating flag clear) and decimal point (indicating\nACK) is just too subtle, IMHO.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2025-12-27T11:04:33.603Z",
